# Line endings.
#
# This repository is authored on Windows and built on Linux (GitHub Actions, EAS, Vercel).
# Without this file every checkout on one platform rewrites the working tree of the other, and
# `git diff` fills with whole-file changes that contain no change at all.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF in the object store and checks out LF everywhere. LF rather
# than native, because three things here care about the byte:
#
#   * shell scripts inside .github/workflows heredocs — bash refuses a CRLF `SQL` terminator
#   * supabase/migrations/*.sql, replayed by psql in CI
#   * services/anomaly shell entrypoints in the Docker image
*                    text=auto eol=lf

# Binary. Never diffed, never normalised — a "text" PNG is a corrupted PNG.
*.png                binary
*.jpg                binary
*.jpeg               binary
*.gif                binary
*.ico                binary
*.webp               binary
*.pdf                binary
*.ttf                binary
*.otf                binary
*.woff               binary
*.woff2              binary
*.joblib             binary
*.pkl                binary

# Generated, and enormous. Collapsed in pull requests so a dependency bump does not bury the
# change it came with; still versioned, because a lockfile that is not is not a lockfile.
package-lock.json    linguist-generated=true -diff

# GitHub's language stats otherwise report this project as majority SQL, because the migrations
# are long and heavily commented. They are the most important files here, but they are not what
# the repository is written in.
supabase/migrations/*.sql linguist-detectable=true linguist-language=PLpgSQL
